    {
      "bbox": [
        131,
        1094,
        1468,
        1664
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Section 1. Pursuant to \u00a7 24-605 of the Administrative Code of the City of New York, the Fire Department is designated the agency authorized to receive and file with the City Collector certificates of expenses for Fire Department costs incurred in responding to emergencies involving a release or substantial threat of a release of a hazardous substance into the environment. Such certificates shall be prepared in accordance with \u00a7 24-606 of the Administrative Code, shall set forth the work done and the expenses incurred, shall certify that such expenses were necessary and proper in the exercise of the Department's lawful powers and shall, where applicable, apportion such expenses among lots or buildings belonging to different persons. Pursuant to \u00a7 24-605, such costs shall constitute a lien against the real property at which such response measures were implemented.",
